`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Documented constraints."})," Chaos Visual Debugger records simulation state. Its ReSim badge identifies frames recorded during network correction; rerunning simulations/queries inside CVD is listed as future work. Async game frames and solver frames need not correspond one-to-one; the game timeline chooses the closest solver timestamp. Solver-stage inspection depends on recorded channels. Contact selections expire across frames and may display stale data with a warning. Joint, character-ground-constraint and acceleration-structure recording are disabled by default. Recorded particle geometry is physics-thread geometry, which may differ from game-thread geometry. Component queries have limited support. Rapid landscape collision unload/reload can display incorrectly while scrubbing; the documented workaround is reloading the recording. These are UE 5.5 guide limitations, not claims about later releases. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://dev.epicgames.com/documentation/en-us/unreal-engine/chaos-visual-debugger-user-guide?application_version=5.5",children:"Official UE 5.5 guide"})]}),`
