`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Proposed acceptance."})," Retain ordered body/subshape identities, base offset, relative and reconstructed world points, normal convention, signed depth and update identity. Use an asymmetric two-body fixture with an origin shift to catch swapped normals and dropped offsets. Classify speculative contacts separately from resolved impacts. Do not present one retained subshape pair as an exhaustive collision-feature inventory."]}),`
