`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["In the ordinary Rigidbody connection path, ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"Joint.connectedBody"})," is the endpoint reference; leaving it unset connects to a fixed world point. Unity does not support that connection across a different Scene using a local physics Scene. Moving the connected Rigidbody into a Scene using ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"LocalPhysicsMode.Physics3D"})," automatically disconnects it. An intended pair remaining visually adjacent therefore does not establish a surviving connection. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.0/Documentation/ScriptReference/Joint-connectedBody.html",children:"Connected-body API"})]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.code,{children:"Joint.anchor"})," uses local coordinates. ConfigurableJoint exposes per-axis linear/angular motion modes, limits, drive mode and target values; ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"configuredInWorldSpace"})," changes the target-value frame. Preserve the two endpoint identities, physics-scene identities, anchors, axis basis, motion restrictions and chosen target frame as inputs rather than deriving them from a screenshot. The exposed properties are configuration, not a native motion-completed result. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.0/Documentation/ScriptReference/Joint-anchor.html",children:"Anchor API"}),", ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.0/Documentation/ScriptReference/ConfigurableJoint.html",children:"ConfigurableJoint API"})]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["ArticulationBody instead describes a reduced-coordinate logical tree. Its ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"parentAnchorPosition"})," is relative to the parent ",e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"articulation body"}),", which can differ from the immediate Transform parent when intermediate nodes exist. The revolute axis is the parent anchor's X axis, and rotating that anchor changes the axis in world space. This requires an explicit body/anchor hierarchy map, not only a scene-Transform list. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.0/Documentation/ScriptReference/ArticulationBody.html",children:"Articulation API"}),", ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.0/Documentation/ScriptReference/ArticulationBody-parentAnchorPosition.html",children:"Parent-anchor API"}),", ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.0/Documentation/Manual/class-ArticulationBody.html",children:"Articulation component reference"})]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h5,{id:"2-keep-requested-targets-units-and-measured-motion-separate",children:"2. Keep requested targets, units and measured motion separate"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The articulation component reference describes drives as implicit springs with position-error and velocity-error terms. The force limit caps generated force/torque. Zero stiffness removes position attraction; zero damping does not make the drive stop at its target. A drive target is therefore not a settling or interaction-success signal. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.0/Documentation/Manual/class-ArticulationBody.html",children:"Articulation component reference"})]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The documented angular units differ by interface: ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"ArticulationDrive.target"})," uses ",e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"degrees"}),", while ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"SetDriveTargets(List<float>)"})," and ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"GetJointPositions(List<float>)"})," use ",e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"radians"}),"; their linear quantities use meters. ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"GetJointVelocities(List<float>)"})," documents meters/second and radians/second. These are documentation-level contracts requiring exact-build verification, not measured implementation behavior. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.0/Documentation/ScriptReference/ArticulationDrive-target.html",children:"Per-drive target"}),", ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.0/Documentation/ScriptReference/ArticulationBody.SetDriveTargets.html",children:"Bulk target setter"}),", ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.0/Documentation/ScriptReference/ArticulationBody.GetJointPositions.html",children:"Position readback"}),", ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.0/Documentation/ScriptReference/ArticulationBody.GetJointVelocities.html",children:"Velocity readback"})]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.code,{children:"SetDriveTargets"})," returns void and addresses the whole hierarchy. ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"GetDofStartIndices(List<int>)"})," supplies offsets indexed by each body's ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"index"}),"; that body's ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"dofCount"})," supplies its span. The integer result is the hierarchy's total DOF count, not a success code. Do not assume one float per scene node, infer stable correspondence from equal array lengths, or reuse an old mapping after topology/lock changes without validation. The inspected documentation does not specify malformed-buffer error behavior, transactional application or cancellation. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.0/Documentation/ScriptReference/ArticulationBody.SetDriveTargets.html",children:"Bulk target setter"}),", ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.0/Documentation/ScriptReference/ArticulationBody.GetDofStartIndices.html",children:"DOF mapping"})]}),`
